\f0\b\fs24 \cf0 Chapter 38 - Postcards from a failed universe
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx4565\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 After managing to blame his underlings for blowing up his lab, The Johnn is set up in another lab at a remote location - An old underground railway station that had been converted into a bomb shelter. They have done every conceivable test upon the discs and decide to give spinning the discs another lash. 
\f1 \

\f2 At that moment Sarah experiences the first labour pains - she gets a message/feeling from the child (Richard) that he wanted to be born immediately. She is blasted with images of Johnny in his lab accompanied by feelings of dread/fear.
\f1 \

\f2 \
Sarah visits the office with Richard and tells Det Lanning she has some sort of telepathic link with Richard. She tells of all the imagery and raw feelings emitted from him. Hayley says she has received some disturbing reports from Johnny\'92s lab-techs including their plans to spin the dics again and Hayley threatens to terminate his contract. Sarah is sent to the lab to supervise the progress of the research.
\f1 \
\pard\tx4565\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 - - -
\f1 \
\pard\tx4565\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 Sarah, Dr Logan and Cracker visit the lab and lay down the law to Johnny. He says he has plans to spin both the discs at once. One clockwise and the other anti-clockwise assuming they would cancel each other out. He gets nothing but grief from Sarah and Dr Logan and sets the dics spinning. He says he can\'92t turn it off, it has to cycle through. Inside the bunker the discs started shooting blue lightening - sandbags lining the bunker begin to fly around and explode, setting the sand crystal alight. Some sandbags smashed into the gap between the dics and disappeared into the ether.
\f1 \

\f2 Gravity shifts towards the bunker, at 45 degrees inside the control room. Sarah desperately tries to shit down th program, but can\'92t. The system shuts down by itself. Cracker had shut off the power, but he claims it wasn\'92t his idea - someow Richard \'93told\'94 him what to do.
